WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.054 --> 00:00:10.030
In the early days of July, Pollyanna read aloud, studied cooking and sewing, and practiced the piano.

2
00:00:10.031 --> 00:00:15.691
But she also had four hours every afternoon to "just live."

3
00:00:15.692 --> 00:00:20.542
It was unclear why Pollyanna had been given all this free time.

4
00:00:20.543 --> 00:00:26.007
Was Aunt Polly giving her a break from the other activities?

5
00:00:26.008 --> 00:00:33.493
Or was Aunt Polly herself taking a break—from Pollyanna?

6
00:00:33.494 --> 00:00:37.257
Either way, Pollyanna enjoyed her afternoons.

7
00:00:37.258 --> 00:00:42.683
The Harrington house was on the edge of town, and no children lived nearby.

8
00:00:42.684 --> 00:00:48.500
This didn't bother Pollyanna, who enjoyed walking around town, observing people.

9
00:00:48.501 --> 00:00:55.509
On these walks, she often ran into a man who was usually alone.

10
00:00:55.510 --> 00:01:03.100
Feeling sorry for him one day, Pollyanna said cheerfully, "How are you, sir? It's a nice day!"

11
00:01:03.101 --> 00:01:08.272
The man glanced around. "Did you just speak to me?"

12
00:01:08.273 --> 00:01:10.466
"Yes, sir, I said—"

13
00:01:10.467 --> 00:01:13.551
The man grunted and walked away.

14
00:01:13.552 --> 00:01:19.586
Pollyanna laughed. "What a funny fellow!"

15
00:01:19.587 --> 00:01:24.824
When she spoke to him the next day, he grunted again.

16
00:01:24.825 --> 00:01:29.245
But the third time she greeted him, he stopped abruptly.

17
00:01:29.246 --> 00:01:33.879
"Who are you, and why are you speaking to me?" the man demanded.

18
00:01:33.880 --> 00:01:41.080
"I'm Pollyanna Whittier, and I thought you looked lonely." Pollyanna smiled.

19
00:01:41.081 --> 00:01:45.267
"I've told you my name, but I don't know yours."

20
00:01:45.268 --> 00:01:49.803
The man scowled and walked away faster than ever.

21
00:01:49.804 --> 00:01:55.772
Pollyanna's smile faded, but she kept walking.

22
00:01:55.773 --> 00:02:00.921
When she arrived home, Nancy was grumbling about doing an errand for Aunt Polly.

23
00:02:00.922 --> 00:02:09.361
"How I hate visiting Mrs. Snow!" Nancy was packing a container of beef stew into a basket.

24
00:02:09.362 --> 00:02:15.019
"She complains all the time. Even the days of the week make her unhappy.

25
00:02:15.020 --> 00:02:18.223
If it's Tuesday, she wishes it were Wednesday.

26
00:02:18.224 --> 00:02:22.837
I feel sorry for her daughter, Milly, who takes care of her."

27
00:02:22.838 --> 00:02:26.418
"Who's Mrs. Snow?" Pollyanna asked.

28
00:02:26.419 --> 00:02:29.938
"An invalid who belongs to Miss Polly's church.

29
00:02:29.939 --> 00:02:34.311
Miss Polly thinks it's her duty to send Mrs. Snow some food every week.

30
00:02:34.312 --> 00:02:38.407
But she doesn't do it herself—she sends me."

31
00:02:38.408 --> 00:02:43.995
"Mrs. Snow sounds different. I love people who are different!

32
00:02:43.996 --> 00:02:47.215
I'll be happy to take the stew to her."

33
00:02:47.216 --> 00:02:52.053
"But you just came home," Nancy protested weakly.

34
00:02:52.054 --> 00:02:55.202
"I'd be glad to go out again."

35
00:02:55.203 --> 00:03:01.099
Pollyanna reached for the basket, and Nancy handed it over.

36
00:03:01.100 --> 00:03:06.298
Half an hour later, Pollyanna was standing in Mrs. Snow's darkened bedroom.

37
00:03:06.299 --> 00:03:12.968
When her eyes adjusted to the gloom, she saw a woman half–sitting up in bed.

38
00:03:12.969 --> 00:03:19.562
"Hello, Mrs. Snow, I've brought some beef stew from my aunt Polly."

39
00:03:19.563 --> 00:03:25.513
"Beef stew? I'm grateful, of course, but I was hoping for chicken soup today.

40
00:03:25.514 --> 00:03:28.066
I didn't sleep a wink last night and—"

41
00:03:28.067 --> 00:03:33.026
"I wish I didn't have to sleep!" Pollyanna sighed.

42
00:03:33.027 --> 00:03:38.694
"It's such a waste of time when you could be just living."

43
00:03:38.695 --> 00:03:43.068
The woman sat up straight and peered at Pollyanna.

44
00:03:43.069 --> 00:03:50.630
"Aren't you an amazing child! Open the curtains, so I can get a look at you."

45
00:03:50.631 --> 00:03:59.311
"Oh dear, now you'll see my freckles." Pollyanna went over to the window.

46
00:03:59.312 --> 00:04:04.657
"Oh!" Pollyanna exclaimed as she turned toward Mrs. Snow.

47
00:04:04.658 --> 00:04:09.582
"I'm glad you wanted to see me because now I can see you!

48
00:04:09.583 --> 00:04:13.920
Nobody told me you were so pretty."

49
00:04:13.921 --> 00:04:17.249
"Me, pretty?"

50
00:04:17.250 --> 00:04:26.056
"Yes, your eyes are so big and dark, and you have beautiful black curly hair. Let me show you."

51
00:04:26.057 --> 00:04:30.326
Pollyanna skipped over to the bureau and picked up a hand mirror.

52
00:04:30.327 --> 00:04:34.365
She stopped and studied Mrs. Snow's face.

53
00:04:34.366 --> 00:04:39.298
"If you don't mind, I'd like to fix your hair a little before you look."

54
00:04:39.299 --> 00:04:42.756
"Well, if you must . . ."

55
00:04:42.757 --> 00:04:46.619
"I love to style hair!"

56
00:04:46.620 --> 00:04:51.364
Pollyanna fluffed out Mrs. Snow's bangs and arranged her curls.

57
00:04:51.365 --> 00:04:55.549
As a finishing touch, she put a pink flower in Mrs. Snow's hair.

58
00:04:55.550 --> 00:05:00.204
Mrs. Snow complained the whole time, but she was secretly excited.

59
00:05:00.205 --> 00:05:04.598
At last Pollyanna handed her the mirror.

60
00:05:04.599 --> 00:05:10.594
"I really prefer red flowers." Mrs. Snow frowned.

61
00:05:10.595 --> 00:05:14.520
"And my hair will never stay this way."

62
00:05:14.521 --> 00:05:19.836
"Then I'd be glad to come back next week and style it again," Pollyanna said.

63
00:05:19.837 --> 00:05:25.707
"It's hard to be glad about anything when you're stuck in bed all day."

64
00:05:25.708 --> 00:05:33.130
"You're right—that is hard. But I'm sure I'll think of something for you to be glad about."

65
00:05:33.131 --> 00:05:36.145
Pollyanna patted Mrs. Snow's arm.

66
00:05:36.146 --> 00:05:41.939
"I must go now, but I've had such a lovely time!"

67
00:05:41.940 --> 00:05:47.288
As soon as Pollyanna left, Mrs. Snow looked in the mirror again.

68
00:05:47.289 --> 00:05:56.680
"I never realized my hair was so pretty!"

